  "conclusion": "Under a pure random walk the newest leaked training label agrees in sign with the test label 79.5% of the time (1/2 + arcsin(0.8)/pi), with no information about the future. On synthetic i.i.d. returns a 1-nearest-neighbour model trained without the purge scores 72.4% (Sharpe 3.67); its nearest neighbour is the newest row in 60% of decisions, and on those it scores 82.6% (a little above the unconditional 79.5%: the newest row is nearest when its one unshared return is small, which makes the two labels even more alike). A 20-tree random forest scores 66.7% with Sharpe 2.85 on noise, against the retracted model's 67.2% and 2.47. With the purge the same models score 50.4% and 50.8%. Block-shuffled real CL=F returns give the same picture (72.9% leaked vs 49.7% purged). The retracted Sharpe was the label overlap, not a forecast.",
